Subject: [PATCH] Load CBoot-trained Jetson TX1 EMC timings

The P2180 CBoot DT contains timings trained for the installed LPDDR4 on
each boot. Keep its DT reserved and read the RAM code 0 nominal and
derated entries for 408, 665.6, and 800 MHz. Leave the reserved-memory
table ABI in place for trees without a CBoot handoff.

Timing property mapping adapted from Aaron Kling’s Tegra210 DT parser.
Link: https://lkml.indiana.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2505.1/00113.html

